diff --git a/docs/guides/deployment-endpoints.md b/docs/guides/deployment-endpoints.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6481b50
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/guides/deployment-endpoints.md
@@ -0,0 +1,63 @@
+# Server endpoints and development authentication
+
+PostgreSQL and native replication are different protocols. A primary listens for
+SQL on `--port` (default 5432) and native WAL on `--replication-port` (default
+5433). Give them distinct endpoints. A standby's `--primary-host` must address
+the primary's native replication port, not its SQL port. PostgreSQL ErrorResponse
+bytes at that endpoint indicate a protocol mismatch; changing retry delays will
+not correct it. Listener bind failures are reported before server readiness.
+
+For example, using separate private test data directories:
+
+```bash
+heliosdb-nano start --data-dir /srv/nano-primary --listen 127.0.0.1 \
+  --port 5432 --replication-role primary --replication-port 5433 --http-port 0
+heliosdb-nano start --data-dir /srv/nano-standby --listen 127.0.0.1 \
+  --port 5442 --replication-role standby --primary-host 127.0.0.1:5433 --http-port 0
+```
+
+Both peers require native protocol v2. A standby verifies dataset history before
+readiness and refuses a replacement history. First startup needs a new, nonexistent
+standby data-directory leaf; do not pre-create it. A successful native connection
+does not prove catchup across a restart or a recreated primary. See the
+[history guard and interface restrictions](replication-history-guard.md) and
+[offline recovery limitations](offline-reseed.md).
+
+The equivalent primary replication configuration is:
+
+```toml
+[replication]
+role = "primary"
+replication_port = 5433
+sync_mode = "async"
+startup_timeout_secs = 30 # 1..=3600; standby DNS and initial history verification
+```
+
+Replication values resolve as explicit CLI flags, then file values, then defaults.
+`--replication-startup-timeout-secs` overrides the standby verification budget,
+including when explicitly set to its 30-second default. Standby daemon readiness
+allows that budget plus 5 seconds.
+Explicit `--replication-role standalone` overrides a configured primary; explicit
+`--standby-hosts ''` clears its configured peer list. Host endpoints accept DNS
+names, IPv4, or bracketed IPv6 with a nonzero port. Unknown replication keys and
+invalid values are errors. `standby_hosts` and `observer_hosts` are arrays; as with
+the existing CLI, these lists do not make tier-1 actively dial those peers.
+
+HTTP accepts a literal IPv4/IPv6 address or an IP:port socket:
+
+```bash
+heliosdb-nano start --memory --http-listen 127.0.0.1:8081
+heliosdb-nano start --memory --http-listen '[::1]:8081'
+```
+
+An explicit `--http-port` overrides a port embedded in `--http-listen`; without
+either, the port is 8080. `--http-port 0` disables HTTP even when the listen value
+contains a port. Bare IPv6 addresses are supported; bracket IPv6 when attaching
+a port. HTTP DNS names are not accepted.
+
+Remote trust authentication remains refused by default. For isolated development,
+`--allow-insecure-trust` explicitly permits PostgreSQL trust on a non-loopback
+interface and emits an insecure-development warning. It does not change the
+selected authentication method; password/SCRAM authentication remains enforced
+when selected. The option is preserved in daemon mode. Prefer loopback or password
+authentication for ordinary deployments.
diff --git a/docs/guides/offline-reseed.md b/docs/guides/offline-reseed.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..dbccfbc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/guides/offline-reseed.md
@@ -0,0 +1,100 @@
+# Recovering a snapshot after a primary is recreated
+
+A recreated primary is a new authoritative dataset. Never attach an old standby's
+rows or WAL position to it by deleting a marker, resetting an LSN, or simply
+restarting streaming. Preserve the old standby until the recovered data has been
+checked and the operator has selected which history to keep.
+
+Nano does **not** currently provide an online `resync` / `basebackup` protocol with
+a coherent snapshot-to-WAL boundary. The helper below prepares a full **offline
+physical snapshot into a new directory**. It does not enable streaming or claim
+that reconnecting this snapshot will catch up safely. Issue #7's online recovery
+request remains open.
+
+## Prepare an offline snapshot
+
+Use the same Nano binary/version and compatible storage configuration on both
+hosts. This procedure supports a local Linux POSIX filesystem and a normal
+RocksDB-backed data directory. Network filesystems, externally stored database
+files, live filesystem copies, and running embedded processes are outside this
+procedure. Preserve any encryption keys separately and securely; the helper does
+not reconstruct external configuration or key material.
+
+1. Fence application writes and cleanly stop both the primary and old standby
+   through their service manager or exact owned PID. Keep their old data paths.
+   A lock can detect an open database; it cannot prove a prior shutdown was clean.
+   After a crash, first recover the primary using Nano and then stop it cleanly.
+2. On the primary host, run the repository helper with an unused destination:
+
+   ```bash
+   python3 scripts/nano-offline-reseed.py \
+     --source /srv/nano-primary \
+     --target /srv/nano-snapshot-20260929 \
+     --confirm-offline
+   ```
+
+   The confirmation acknowledges that all writers remain stopped for this copy;
+   it does not bypass the database lock. The helper holds the same whole-file
+   POSIX `fcntl` lock on `LOCK` that RocksDB uses. `flock` alone would not exclude
+   Nano. It refuses an existing destination (even an empty one), nested paths,
+   symlinks, hard-linked files and nonregular entries. It copies to a private
+   staging directory, checks SHA-256 bytes against the locked source, syncs files,
+   then publishes with atomic no-replace rename. Failed partial copies are left
+   under a clearly named `.reseed-*.partial` directory, never at the target path.
+3. If transferring to another host, transfer this stopped snapshot in full into
+   another unused path over an authenticated channel. Verify the SHA-256 entries
+   in `NANO-OFFLINE-SNAPSHOT.json` **before** opening it. Keep directory access
+   restricted. The manifest is local provenance, not a cryptographic signature.
+4. Inspect the copied database with the same Nano version, in standalone mode
+   and isolated from application routing. Validate schema, row counts, important
+   data, constraints and indexes. Opening a database can legitimately alter its
+   WAL/files, so manifest checks belong before opening it. Keep the primary and
+   old standby intact until validation succeeds.
+
+This creates a candidate recovered dataset for controlled standalone operation.
+It does **not** yet create a certified streaming standby. Do not resume application
+writes on the assumption that this helper made HA safe. A physical copy preserves
+internal row keys, index data, RocksDB WAL and metadata as one stopped state; a
+logical dump is not an interchangeable native replication baseline.
+
+The [native history guard](replication-history-guard.md) now refuses unrelated
+history and unbound pre-existing receiver paths. This helper deliberately does
+not manufacture a receiver binding or authorize its output for streaming.
+
+## What blocks an online standby rebuild
+
+At the campaign base `916138311c69f1cde070fb3d53fc601e22cc0a06`:
+
+- The native handshake identifies a node, but has no durable database-history /
+  timeline identity tied to the data directory. A newly generated node UUID is
+  not a snapshot/history proof.
+- `StreamingClient::new` and the WAL applicator initialize applied LSN to zero.
+  There is no durable snapshot manifest binding a checkpoint to that receiver.
+- Storage-origin broadcasts go through `HAState::broadcast_wal_entry`; that path
+  does not durably append to the streaming server's `WalStore` or advance its
+  private `current_lsn`. The CLI also constructed this store at `./data/wal`
+  independently of `--data-dir`. Fixing its path alone cannot repair history.
+- The binary dump interface does not export all physical/index state or an
+  atomic native replication checkpoint. Restoring a logical dump and replaying
+  WAL from zero can duplicate or misapply operations.
+
+Before offering online resync, the protocol needs a coherent snapshot boundary,
+durable history identity, durable applied/flush positions, retained WAL covering
+the snapshot-to-current interval, and rejection of a missing interval or unrelated
+history. End-to-end tests must cover reconnect, restart, truncation, primary
+replacement, transactional visibility, and post-snapshot changes. A healthy
+handshake or matching row count before new writes is insufficient.
+
+## Regression checks
+
+```bash
+python3 scripts/test_nano_offline_reseed.py
+# Heavy Rust gate: use the shared-host build lock and bounded scope.
+cargo test --test offline_reseed_tests
+```
+
+The Python suite checks refusal and file preservation, including a separate
+process holding RocksDB's lock primitive. The Rust suite checks refusal against
+an actual open Nano instance and reopening a stopped copy with rows, uniqueness
+constraints and independent subsequent writes. Neither suite certifies online
+replication continuation.
diff --git a/examples/bench_live_replay.rs b/examples/bench_live_replay.rs
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f2bd55f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/examples/bench_live_replay.rs
@@ -0,0 +1,356 @@
+//! EXTERNAL DRAFT. Copy unchanged to examples/ only after the owning gate ends.
+//! Run release-only, one process at a time under the shared fleet lock/scope.
+//! Times real WAL decode + live row application, excluding primary SQL setup,
+//! validation, network, queue bookkeeping, and commit acknowledgment durability.
+use heliosdb_nano::{
+    config::WalSyncModeConfig,
+    storage::{WalOperation, WalSyncMode, WriteAheadLog},
+    Config, EmbeddedDatabase, Tuple, Value,
+};
+use serde_json::{json, Value as Json};
+use sha2::{Digest, Sha256};
+use std::{
+    fs::{self, File, OpenOptions},
+    io::{BufWriter, Write},
+    path::{Path, PathBuf},
+    time::{Instant, SystemTime, UNIX_EPOCH},
+};
+
+type Outcome<T> = Result<T, Box<dyn std::error::Error>>;
+const TABLE: &str = "replay_perf";
+const WARM: &str = "SELECT id, grp, payload FROM replay_perf ORDER BY id";
+
+struct Report {
+    out: BufWriter<File>,
+}
+impl Report {
+    fn record(&mut self, value: Json) -> Outcome<()> {
+        serde_json::to_writer(&mut self.out, &value)?;
+        self.out.write_all(b"\n")?;
+        self.out.flush()?;
+        Ok(())
+    }
+}
+
+fn load() -> Outcome<f64> {
+    Ok(fs::read_to_string("/proc/loadavg")?
+        .split_whitespace()
+        .next()
+        .ok_or("missing Linux load average")?
+        .parse()?)
+}
+fn epoch_ms() -> Outcome<u128> {
+    Ok(SystemTime::now().duration_since(UNIX_EPOCH)?.as_millis())
+}
+fn numbers(tuple: &Tuple) -> Outcome<Vec<i64>> {
+    tuple
+        .values
+        .iter()
+        .map(|v| match v {
+            Value::Int2(n) => Ok(i64::from(*n)),
+            Value::Int4(n) => Ok(i64::from(*n)),
+            Value::Int8(n) => Ok(*n),
+            other => Err(format!("unexpected non-integer result {other:?}").into()),
+        })
+        .collect()
+}
+fn query(db: &EmbeddedDatabase, sql: &str) -> Outcome<Vec<Vec<i64>>> {
+    db.query(sql, &[])?.iter().map(numbers).collect()
+}
+fn expected(n: usize, phase: &str) -> Vec<Vec<i64>> {
+    if phase == "empty" || phase == "delete" {
+        return Vec::new();
+    }
+    (1..=n as i64)
+        .map(|id| {
+            if phase == "update" {
+                vec![id, (id + 1) % 64, id * 10 + 1]
+            } else {
+                vec![id, id % 64, id * 10]
+            }
+        })
+        .collect()
+}
+fn database(path: &Path, storage: &str) -> Outcome<EmbeddedDatabase> {
+    let mut config = if storage == "memory" {
+        Config::in_memory()
+    } else {
+        Config::default()
+    };
+    if storage == "disk" {
+        config.storage.path = Some(path.to_path_buf());
+    }
+    config.storage.wal_enabled = true;
+    // Forces real per-statement WAL capture without process-global HA role state.
+    config.storage.logical_wal_per_statement = true;
+    config.storage.wal_sync_mode = WalSyncModeConfig::Async;
+    config.storage.wal_checkpoint_on_close = false;
+    config.storage.wal_checkpoint_interval_entries = 0;
+    config.storage.wal_checkpoint_interval_secs = 0;
+    let db = EmbeddedDatabase::with_config(config)?;
+    db.execute("CREATE TABLE replay_perf (id INT PRIMARY KEY, grp INT, payload INT UNIQUE)")?;
+    db.execute("CREATE INDEX replay_perf_grp ON replay_perf(grp)")?;
+    Ok(db)
+}
+
+// All query observations, including failures and full actual/expected row sets,
+// are written outside the timing interval. Failure never becomes a valid sample.
+fn validate(db: &EmbeddedDatabase, want: &[Vec<i64>], label: &str, report: &mut Report) -> Outcome<bool> {
+    let raw = db.storage.scan_table(TABLE)?;
+    let mut raw_values: Vec<Vec<i64>> = raw.iter().map(numbers).collect::<Outcome<_>>()?;
+    raw_values.sort();
+    let mut sorted_want = want.to_vec();
+    sorted_want.sort();
+    let mut valid = raw_values == sorted_want;
+    report.record(json!({"kind":"validation", "stage":label, "probe":"raw_storage",
+        "valid":valid, "expected":sorted_want, "actual":raw_values,
+        "row_ids":raw.iter().map(|row| row.row_id).collect::<Vec<_>>()}))?;
+    let mut probes = vec![
+        (WARM.to_string(), want.to_vec()),
+        (
+            "SELECT payload, grp, id FROM replay_perf WHERE id > 0 ORDER BY id".into(),
+            want.iter().map(|row| vec![row[2], row[1], row[0]]).collect(),
+        ),
+        ("SELECT COUNT(*) FROM replay_perf".into(), vec![vec![want.len() as i64]]),
+    ];
+    for id in [1, want.len() as i64 / 2 + 1, want.len().max(1) as i64] {
+        probes.push((
+            format!("SELECT id, grp, payload FROM replay_perf WHERE id = {id}"),
+            want.iter().filter(|row| row[0] == id).cloned().collect(),
+        ));
+    }
+    for group in [0, 7, 63] {
+        probes.push((
+            format!("SELECT id, grp, payload FROM replay_perf WHERE grp = {group} ORDER BY id"),
+            want.iter().filter(|row| row[1] == group).cloned().collect(),
+        ));
+    }
+    // Check both old and new keys in the unique payload index.
+    for payload in [10, 11] {
+        probes.push((
+            format!("SELECT id, grp, payload FROM replay_perf WHERE payload = {payload}"),
+            want.iter().filter(|row| row[2] == payload).cloned().collect(),
+        ));
+    }
+    for (sql, expected) in probes {
+        match query(db, &sql) {
+            Ok(actual) => {
+                let pass = actual == expected;
+                valid &= pass;
+                report.record(json!({"kind":"validation", "stage":label, "sql":sql,
+                    "valid":pass, "expected":expected, "actual":actual}))?;
+            }
+            Err(error) => {
+                valid = false;
+                report.record(json!({"kind":"validation", "stage":label, "sql":sql,
+                    "valid":false, "expected":expected, "error":error.to_string()}))?;
+            }
+        }
+    }
+    Ok(valid)
+}
+
+fn prepare(primary: &EmbeddedDatabase, n: usize, phase: &str, report: &mut Report) -> Outcome<Vec<Vec<u8>>> {
+    let before = primary.storage.wal_lsn().ok_or("logical WAL unavailable")?;
+    let timer = Instant::now();
+    for id in 1..=n {
+        let sql = match phase {
+            "insert" => format!("INSERT INTO replay_perf VALUES ({id}, {}, {})", id % 64, id * 10),
+            "update" => format!(
+                "UPDATE replay_perf SET grp = {}, payload = {} WHERE id = {id}",
+                (id + 1) % 64,
+                id * 10 + 1
+            ),
+            "delete" => format!("DELETE FROM replay_perf WHERE id = {id}"),
+            _ => return Err("unknown benchmark phase".into()),
+        };
+        primary.execute(&sql)?;
+    }
+    let reader = WriteAheadLog::open(primary.storage.db(), WalSyncMode::Async)?;
+    let entries = reader.replay_from(before)?;
+    let mut row_operations = 0;
+    let mut operations = Vec::new();
+    for entry in entries {
+        let variant_matches = match (&entry.operation, phase) {
+            (WalOperation::Insert { table, .. }, "insert")
+            | (WalOperation::Update { table, .. }, "update")
+            | (WalOperation::Delete { table, .. }, "delete") => table == TABLE,
+            _ => false,
+        };
+        if variant_matches {
+            row_operations += 1;
+        } else if !matches!(&entry.operation, WalOperation::UpdateCounter { table_name, .. } if table_name == TABLE) {
+            return Err(format!("unexpected SQL-generated {phase} WAL operation {:?}", entry.operation).into());
+        }
+        operations.push(bincode::serialize(&entry.operation)?);
+    }
+    if row_operations != n {
+        return Err(format!("{phase}: expected {n} real row records, got {row_operations}").into());
+    }
+    report.record(
+        json!({"kind":"preparation", "phase":phase, "row_operations":row_operations,
+        "wal_records":operations.len(), "serialized_bytes":operations.iter().map(Vec::len).sum::<usize>(),
+        "elapsed_ns":timer.elapsed().as_nanos(), "excluded_from_apply_timing":true}),
+    )?;
+    let wanted = expected(n, phase);
+    if !validate(primary, &wanted, &format!("primary_{phase}"), report)? {
+        return Err("primary fixture SQL is not correct; refuse to time replay".into());
+    }
+    Ok(operations)
+}
+
+fn trial(n: usize, storage: &str, root: &Path, report: &mut Report) -> Outcome<bool> {
+    let primary = database(&root.join("primary"), storage)?;
+    let standby = database(&root.join("standby"), storage)?;
+    let mut previous = "empty";
+    let mut all_valid = true;
+    let mut maximum_replayed_row_id = 0;
+    for phase in ["insert", "update", "delete"] {
+        let operations = prepare(&primary, n, phase, report)?;
+        let before_rows = expected(n, previous);
+        let mut pre_valid = validate(&standby, &before_rows, &format!("standby_before_{phase}"), report)?;
+        for attempt in 1..=5 {
+            let actual = query(&standby, WARM)?;
+            let valid = actual == before_rows;
+            pre_valid &= valid;
+            report.record(json!({"kind":"cache_warm", "phase":phase, "attempt":attempt,
+                "sql":WARM, "valid":valid, "expected":before_rows, "actual":actual}))?;
+        }
+        let load_before = load()?;
+        if load_before >= 6.0 {
+            report.record(json!({"kind":"load_gate_refusal", "phase":phase, "load1":load_before}))?;
+            return Err("load1 must be below 6 before each timed phase; rerun this trial under the fleet gate".into());
+        }
+        let started_ms = epoch_ms()?;
+        let mut raw_chunks: Vec<(usize, u128)> = Vec::with_capacity(operations.len().div_ceil(256));
+        let timer = Instant::now();
+        let mut chunk_start = Instant::now();
+        for (index, bytes) in operations.iter().enumerate() {
+            let operation: WalOperation = bincode::deserialize(bytes)?;
+            if let Err(error) = standby.storage.apply_replicated_operation(operation) {
+                report.record(json!({"kind":"application_error", "phase":phase, "record_index":index,
+                    "elapsed_ns":timer.elapsed().as_nanos(), "eligible_for_comparison":false,
+                    "error":error.to_string()}))?;
+                return Err(error.into());
+            }
+            if (index + 1) % 256 == 0 || index + 1 == operations.len() {
+                raw_chunks.push((index + 1, chunk_start.elapsed().as_nanos()));
+                chunk_start = Instant::now();
+            }
+        }
+        let elapsed_ns = timer.elapsed().as_nanos();
+        let load_after = load()?;
+        // Retain the raw measurement even if later validation itself errors.
+        report.record(json!({"kind":"raw_timing", "phase":phase, "rows":n,
+            "wal_records":operations.len(), "elapsed_ns":elapsed_ns,
+            "rows_per_second":(n as f64)*1e9/(elapsed_ns as f64),
+            "raw_chunk_fields":["end_record", "elapsed_ns"], "raw_chunks":raw_chunks,
+            "started_unix_ms":started_ms, "load1_before":load_before, "load1_after":load_after,
+            "eligible_for_comparison":false, "validation_pending":true,
+            "scope":"bincode decode plus sequential live apply; no network or acknowledged fsync"}))?;
+        let post_valid = validate(&standby, &expected(n, phase), &format!("standby_after_{phase}"), report)?;
+        let valid = pre_valid && post_valid && load_after < 6.0;
+        all_valid &= valid;
+        report.record(json!({"kind":"timing_verdict", "phase":phase,
+            "elapsed_ns":elapsed_ns, "precondition_valid":pre_valid, "postcondition_valid":post_valid,
+            "eligible_for_comparison":valid, "eligibility_also_requires_final_trial_pass":true}))?;
+        if phase == "insert" {
+            maximum_replayed_row_id = standby
+                .storage
+                .scan_table(TABLE)?
+                .iter()
+                .filter_map(|row| row.row_id)
+                .max()
+                .ok_or("missing replayed row IDs")?;
+        }
+        previous = phase;
+    }
+    standby.execute(&format!(
+        "INSERT INTO replay_perf VALUES ({}, 0, {})",
+        n + 1,
+        (n + 1) * 10
+    ))?;
+    let after_promotion = standby.storage.scan_table(TABLE)?;
+    let counter_valid = after_promotion.len() == 1
+        && after_promotion[0].row_id.is_some_and(|id| id > maximum_replayed_row_id)
+        && numbers(&after_promotion[0])? == vec![n as i64 + 1, 0, (n as i64 + 1) * 10];
+    all_valid &= counter_valid;
+    report.record(json!({"kind":"counter_continuation", "valid":counter_valid,
+        "maximum_replayed_row_id":maximum_replayed_row_id,
+        "actual_row_ids":after_promotion.iter().map(|row| row.row_id).collect::<Vec<_>>(),
+        "actual_rows":after_promotion.iter().map(numbers).collect::<Outcome<Vec<_>>>()?}))?;
+    Ok(all_valid)
+}
+
+fn run() -> Outcome<bool> {
+    if cfg!(debug_assertions) {
+        return Err("release build required".into());
+    }
+    let mut args = std::env::args().skip(1);
+    let mut options = std::collections::HashMap::new();
+    while let Some(key) = args.next() {
+        if !matches!(
+            key.as_str(),
+            "--output-dir" | "--label" | "--source-id" | "--rows" | "--storage" | "--round"
+        ) {
+            return Err(format!("unknown argument {key}").into());
+        }
+        let value = args.next().ok_or("each argument requires a value")?;
+        if options.insert(key, value).is_some() {
+            return Err("duplicate argument".into());
+        }
+    }
+    let option = |key: &str| options.get(key).cloned().ok_or_else(|| format!("missing {key}"));
+    let n: usize = option("--rows")?.parse()?;
+    if n == 0 || n > 100_000 {
+        return Err("rows must be in 1..=100000".into());
+    }
+    let storage = option("--storage")?;
+    if storage != "disk" && storage != "memory" {
+        return Err("storage must be disk or memory".into());
+    }
+    let round: usize = option("--round")?.parse()?;
+    let output_dir = PathBuf::from(option("--output-dir")?);
+    fs::create_dir_all(&output_dir)?;
+    let root = tempfile::Builder::new()
+        .prefix("live-replay-perf-")
+        .tempdir_in(&output_dir)?
+        .keep();
+    let path = root.join("observations.jsonl");
+    let mut report = Report {
+        out: BufWriter::new(OpenOptions::new().write(true).create_new(true).open(&path)?),
+    };
+    let executable = std::env::current_exe()?;
+    let binary_sha256 = format!("{:x}", Sha256::digest(fs::read(&executable)?));
+    report.record(
+        json!({"kind":"metadata", "label":option("--label")?, "source_id":option("--source-id")?,
+        "rows":n, "storage":storage, "round":round, "release":true, "pid":std::process::id(),
+        "executable":executable, "executable_sha256":binary_sha256, "fixture_root":root,
+        "default_storage_config_except":{"wal_enabled":true,"logical_wal_per_statement":true,
+            "wal_sync_mode":"Async","wal_checkpoint_on_close":false,
+            "wal_checkpoint_interval_entries":0,"wal_checkpoint_interval_secs":0},
+        "indexes":["PRIMARY KEY(id)","UNIQUE(payload)","manual(grp)"],
+        "retention":"disk mode retains both private datasets; memory mode datasets are internal temporary stores",
+        "comparison_rule":"no ratio/performance acceptance against any failing baseline trial"}),
+    )?;
+    let result = trial(n, &storage, &root, &mut report);
+    match &result {
+        Ok(valid) => report.record(json!({"kind":"outcome", "passed":valid,
+            "eligible_for_comparison":valid, "report":path}))?,
+        Err(error) => report.record(json!({"kind":"outcome", "passed":false,
+            "eligible_for_comparison":false,"error":error.to_string(),"report":path}))?,
+    }
+    report.out.get_ref().sync_all()?;
+    println!("{}", json!({"report":path,"passed":matches!(&result,Ok(true))}));
+    result
+}
+fn main() {
+    match run() {
+        Ok(true) => (),
+        Ok(false) => std::process::exit(1),
+        Err(error) => {
+            eprintln!("live replay benchmark error: {error}");
+            std::process::exit(2);
+        }
+    }
+}
